## Interface: 16001
## Title: Navigation
## Notes: Sane UI's minimap and map in one window. Small in the screen's top right corner it is the minimap; move the mouse into that corner and it fills the screen as the map. Drag it, zoom it with the mouse wheel from a zone out to the whole world, right click for one map out, Ctrl-click for the map pin; draw it as Parchment (Blizzard's maps joined into one), as Scrying (the land as it lies) or, with the module Atlas, painted. The game's map keys open it. Settings: the page Navigation.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Map_01
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its settings and the command. First: the other files add to that table.
Navigation.lua
# The map's spaces (map, world, the plane it is drawn in), the map tree, the terrain's grid. Knows no frames
Coords.lua
# Where a view looks: its middle, its zoom, following the player, the map its zoom shows. Knows no frames
Camera.lua
# What the game tells while playing: the player, the map pin, group, quests, flights, rares, explored areas. Knows no frames
Live.lua
# The frame the map is drawn in, the same for both views: its layers, the player's place, the mouse
Canvas.lua
# The terrain: the game's minimap textures up close, the module's overview of them further out
Terrain.lua
# The zones that have an outline to cut their map art to (made by dev/tools/terrain-art, not by hand)
Outlines.lua
# Blizzard's map art: the world's, the continent's, the zones' cut to their outlines, and the explored parts
Art.lua
# The view Atlas: the painted map of the module SaneUI_Atlas, found at login, loaded when the view is first drawn
Painted.lua
# Over the map at a fixed size: the player's arrow, the map pin
Marks.lua
# The game's minimap over ours, for its live dots; taken and given back
Hybrid.lua
# The game's map kept closed: its keys and every way to it open ours
Native.lua
# The window: the minimap in the top right corner, the map when it fills the screen
Window.lua
